@page "/"

<PageTitle>TaskFlow</PageTitle>

<div class="home">
    <h1>Welcome to a Simple Task Manager</h1>
    <p class="intro">A simple task manager to keep track of what needs doing and when with a built in calendar.</p>

    <div class="cards">
        <a class="card" href="tasks">
            <h2>Tasks</h2>
            <p>Add, complete, and organise your to-dos. Set a due date and priority for each one, then filter by what's still active or already done.</p>
            <span class="card-link">Go to Tasks →</span>
        </a>

        <a class="card" href="calendar">
            <h2>Calendar</h2>
            <p>See your tasks laid out across the month. Each task appears on its due date, colour-coded by priority, so you can spot busy days at a glance.</p>
            <span class="card-link">Go to Calendar →</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    .home { max-width: 700px; }

    .intro {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .cards {
        display: flex;
        gap: 1rem;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .card {
        flex: 1;
        min-width: 260px;
        background: var(--surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        padding: 1.5rem;
        text-decoration: none;
        color: var(--text);
        transition: border-color 0.15s, transform 0.15s;
    }
    .card:hover {
        border-color: var(--accent);
        transform: translateY(-2px);
    }

    .card h2 {
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    }
    .card p {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: 0.92rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    }
    .card-link {
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        font-weight: 500;
    }
</style>